# Drafted by Gemini (R14 sanctum), edited.

~ prefight
Narrator: Dark channels cut into the stone floor brim with warm blood, smelling of copper and crushed roses.
father_renathyr [weary]: You have walked a long, red road to my altar, travelers. Hush now, Duchess, let us hear them before the tithe is paid.
* [if flag.lethica_painting] Show him Lethica's painting. -> pre_lethica
* [if flag.renathyr_journal] Show him the journal. -> pre_journal
* [Persuasion DC 18] Ask him to stop. -> pre_stop | pre_nope
* We have come to end this. -> pre_fight

~ pre_lethica
father_renathyr [afraid]: Put that away! Those eyes belong to a dead morning, Duchess, do not look at her, we are sworn to the Rose now.
Narrator: His gauntleted hand trembles on the pommel, the old vows cracking like thin ice under his boots.
set honor_lost_known
-> prefight

~ pre_journal
father_renathyr [sad]: My own hand wrote those words when the bells still rang silver. That knight died on the mountain, and only the hunger remained.
Narrator: He stands cold and still as a tomb effigy, haunted by the man he used to be.
set honor_lost_known
-> prefight

~ pre_stop
father_renathyr [sad]: Lay down the blade, you say, and let the mountain sleep? Ah, hear how Duchess weeps in her scabbard: she will not allow it.
-> prefight

~ pre_nope
father_renathyr [weary]: You speak of mercy to a man who traded his soul for a sharper edge. Come, Duchess, they have nothing left to teach us.
-> prefight

~ pre_fight
father_renathyr [angry]: Then kneel at the moat and offer your throats to the Crimson Rose! Sing for them, Duchess!
set renathyr_fight_started
quest crimson_monastery bloody_tears
cutscene mon_phase1
cutscene mon_phase1_2
combat mon_abbot

~ geyser
Narrator: With the abbot's last rattle, the blood in the stone channels boils and roars upward in a scalding red geyser.
Narrator: The torrent catches you like dry leaves, hurling you up through the shattered floor into the cathedral above.
set renathyr_slain
move mon_cathedral_moon:from_sanctum

~ hellfire
cutscene mon_hellfire
cutscene mon_hellfire_2
cutscene mon_hellfire_3
set hellfire_seen
Narrator: The great blade buries itself in the altar as the tallow candles roar into green hellfire, and the red glass twists into a grinning face.
viraxys [smile]: Well struck, my little butcher. My golden knight grew so tiresomely sad, take up his blade, drink my grace, and rule this peak.
* [Insight DC 13] She is a fiend. -> hf_fiend | hf_blind
* [Religion DC 13] Read the blade's echo. -> hf_fiend | hf_blind
* [Cleric] Use Divine Sense on the sword. -> hf_fiend
* Refuse her. -> refuse
* Accept her gift. -> accept1

~ hf_fiend
Narrator: Under the perfume of crushed petals hangs the unmistakable stench of brimstone and the pit. No goddess waits in that glass, only a devil.
-> hellfire

~ hf_blind
Narrator: The velvet voice hums in your teeth and warms your blood, leaving only the promise of strength in the dark.
-> hellfire

~ accept1
viraxys [sly]: Such a hungry hand reaching for the hilt. Are you certain you wish to trade your warm breath for my eternal night?
* Yes. -> accept2
* No. -> hellfire

~ accept2
Narrator: To draw that sword is to leave your companions behind forever, rising hereafter only as a creature of the dark.
* Yes, I accept. -> accept
* No. -> hellfire

~ accept
viraxys [smile]: Then drink deep, my new prior, and let the mountain know its master.
set viraxys_offer = "accepted"
cutscene mon_acceptance
cutscene mon_acceptance_2
sacrifice
set hellfire_done
-> END

~ refuse
set viraxys_offer = "refused"
cutscene mon_refusal
cutscene mon_refusal_2
viraxys [angry]: Small souls with smaller stomach, choking on the feast you earned. Keep your cold ashes, then.
Narrator: The hellfire gutters out and the red windows shatter inward like falling sleet, leaving only the mountain wind.
set hellfire_done
-> END

~ sword_altar
Narrator: Freed from the devil's whisper, the heavy blade sits cold in the split stone of the altar, waiting for a hand to claim it.
give sword_of_the_crimson_abbot
set sword_taken
-> END
